    "Non-GMP Hash.toHex concatenates unpadded integer chunks: source-derived128-bit positive-chunk example [1,35] and [18,3] both serialize123 despite distinct bits. Python model only; original PHP not executed.",
    "GMP toHex uses bin2hex(gmp_export), while fallback uses dechex chunks; leading-zero/byte-width encoding can differ by backend. No backend runtime qualification.",
    "Hash.fromBits validates neither binary alphabet nor recipe/width; equals ignores leading zeroes, distance left-pads widths. Same numerical bits from different hash dimensions/algorithms can compare equal.",
    "Default implementation is DifferenceHash with left>right, unlike references using left<right. PerceptualHash includes DC in64 output bits; average excludesDC from threshold whereas median includesDC. Recipe compatibility cannot be inferred from algorithm name.",
    "BlockHash quick mode uses floor-sized blocks and discards remainder strips; below-grid dimensions yield zero block loops. Precise mode distributes to at most four neighbours, requires independent tiny-input qualification.",
    "Compatibility test reports differing golden values with E_USER_WARNING and expectNotToPerformAssertions; runner warning policy decides failure, no equality assertion.",
